Rack Capacity

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs

Rack Capacity is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime that establishes
per-rack capacity accounting for the Data Center Control Plane: how much
capacity one exact rack generation has left across physical slots, power,
cooling, weight and serviceability, which of those constraints becomes binding
first, and which claims about that capacity must be refused as stale, unknown
or unauthoritative.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Rack Capacity does not collect or transmit any telemetry. It opens no network
sockets, performs no name resolution, and contacts no remote service. All state
it writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the
machine running the software.

